.TH BINGUX-TEXT-EDITOR 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-text-editor \- text and code editor for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-text-editor
.RI [ FILE | URI | new: ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-text-editor
opens the Text Editor window: documents in tabs, colours for about 200
languages, find and replace, any encoding and line ending, and a Markdown
preview.
With no argument it opens the documents of the last session, or a new empty
document, or raises the window when it is already open.
.PP
Only one Text Editor window runs.
A second launch hands its files to the running window, which opens each in a
tab and comes to the front.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE
A file path.
.B ~
and relative paths are accepted.
A file that does not exist yet opens as a new document that is saved there.
.TP
.I URI
.BR file:///path .
.TP
.B new:
A new empty document.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/text-editor.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/bingux/text-editor/
The session, drafts of unsaved documents, recent files and where each file was
left.
.SH DEFAULT EDITOR
The desktop entry lists the common text types.
To open plain text in Text Editor, run:
.PP
.RS
.B xdg\-mime default bingux\-text\-editor.desktop text/plain
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The user guide is
.I /usr/share/doc/bingux-text-editor/text-editor.md
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window closed or the running window took the files; 2 for an
unknown option.
